  "id": "COMPOUND:36832 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound (8S,10R,13S,17S)-17-acetyl-10,13-dimethyl-1,2,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one and the cell line FaDu, through a series of intermediate targets. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecules, including Sphingosine 1-phosphate receptor 4, which is itself a target of several other compounds, including 6-(Hydroxymethyl)-9-methoxyphenazine-1-carboxylic acid and methyl 3,5-dimethoxy-4-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxybenzoate. These intermediates all ultimately target FaDu, indicating a potential pathway where the compound may exert its effects through the activation of Sphingosine 1-phosphate receptors, which are known to be involved in various cellular processes, including cell survival and proliferation. The consistent presence of Sphingosine 1-phosphate receptor 4 as a target across multiple pathways supports the notion that this receptor is a key mediator in the biological activity of the compound, and thus, the compound may act as a modulator of this receptor in FaDu cells. The evidence suggests a plausible mechanism involving receptor activation, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
